WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Inventory summarizes on-hand, reserved, unavailable, and available quantities.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Search for FW-001-NAT, then choose its Add stock entry action.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Receipt with quantity 5 previews adding five delivered units.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Opening stock establishes an initial quantity. Use it for starting balances.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Adjustment exposes a Direction field so you can add or remove on-hand stock.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Damaged moves units from available into unavailable stock without changing physical on-hand stock.

7
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Restocked moves unavailable units back to available. This example has no unavailable units, so the preview is invalid and must not be saved.

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Stock entries lists recorded movements and their purchase-lot links.

